# FigDown — figures as text. Spec: https://github.com/FigDown/figdown

# Reference figure for genre `table` — EXPERIMENTAL constructs ONLY (`CONSTRUCT-STATUS-TIERS`).
# `table` owns no experimental construct: `table`, the `|` row token, `cell`
# and `width` are all normative, and so are the cell addresses, the
# `highlight` flag, the span markers, the alignment colons and the column
# widths. What is left is one keyword the genre HOSTS without owning
# (`chart`, with its `type=`) and the two cross-namespace colour keys.
# Every construct here is OUTSIDE the v0.1 conformance surface and OUTSIDE
# the compatibility promise: the engine accepts it and renders it unchanged,
# but it may change or be withdrawn in a later 0.x WITHOUT a migration entry.
# A portable v0.1 table document uses none of it.
# The normative surface is table.fd — kept separate so a reader can see
# exactly where the promise ends.
figdown 0.1 table
title "Egress drops by sampling window (experimental constructs)"

# `stroke=` (cell border colour) was EXPERIMENTAL until 0.1 and is now
# NORMATIVE (`STROKE-KEY-STATUS`); `color=` (text colour) was RETIRED in the same release
# (`COLOUR-KEY-STATUS`), so the only experimental construct left in this file is `chart`.
class hot "Above the drop watermark" fill=#fee2e2 stroke=#b91c1c

# On the BLOCK `stroke=` is the default border for every cell of the grid.
table drops "Drops per window" stroke=#a8a29e
| Window | Q7 | Q3 | Q0 |
|:-------|---:|---:|---:|
| 00:00  |  4 | 31 | 64 |
| 00:05  |  1 | 22 | 51 |
# On a CELL `stroke=` colours that one cell's border, overriding the block
# default. Written bare like this the mark carries no stated meaning;
# `class=hot` on the line above is the form to prefer (`CATEGORICAL-MEANING-MAPPING`).
cell (1,4) class=hot
cell (2,4) stroke=#b45309

# EXPERIMENTAL — `chart` reads the table AS the data: rows → X, columns → Y,
# numeric cells → Z. It is the one keyword a pure `table` section may host
# without owning it, and the only construct here that adds a second drawing
# to the page rather than recolouring the first.
# `type=bar3d` is the whole option surface — `bar3d` is its only value, so
# `chart drops` alone means the same thing. It was spelled `plot` with
# `kind=bars3d` until 0.1, and `level=` was DELETED.
chart drops type=bar3d
